      &middot; D.R. &middot; 2171.</strong> City of Johannesburg, Register of Persons Buried at West Park
      Cemetery, page 54.</figcaption>
  </figure>

  <div class="note">
    <b>Grave 2171, Dutch Reformed section, West Park.</b> George Downing Mountjoy Booyzen &mdash; the
    S.A.R. clerk who died of a perforated ulcer at Forest Hill on 11 December 1947, three years after his
    wife, leaving six children under twenty. This archive has had <em>&ldquo;buried West Park 14
    Dec&rdquo;</em> since the beginning and never the number.
    <br /><br />
    <b>His mother is at Brixton in grave 9760</b>, seven years earlier, in the same denomination&rsquo;s
    ground at a different cemetery. <b>His brother is at Brixton in grave 6889.</b> The three of them are
    in three separate graves in two cemeteries, which is what happens to a family that arrives on a
    goldfield one at a time.
