    <figcaption class="cap">The consecutive grave-number register, braced as one plot:
      <strong>50 &mdash; DASCHNER, JOSEPH H.</strong> &middot;
      <strong>51 &mdash; DASCHNER, CATHERINE M.S.</strong></figcaption>
  </figure>

  <div class="note">
    <b>He bought two graves and was buried in the first.</b> Four years later his wife went into the
    second.
    <br /><br />
    <b>Catherine M.S. Daschner is CATHARINA MARIA SOPHIA BOOYSEN</b>, born 22 April 1891 and baptised at
    Barkly Oost &mdash; a daughter of Willem Hermanus Booyzen and Kathleen Barry, and
    <b>George Downing Mountjoy Booyzen&rsquo;s own sister</b>. Her estate, <b>TAB MHG 3734/46</b>, is one
    of the six files in the letter sitting at the National Archives in Pretoria; this archive has been
    asking that letter for her parents&rsquo; names. It now knows where she is.
    <br /><br />
    Their infant son <b>George Downing Daschner</b> had gone into <b>Brixton</b> in June 1925, seventeen
    years before his father. <a href="#daschner-1942">The 1942 estate &rarr;</a>
